.policy "drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored" revision 1
.description "Put options on a DRF serializer's declared field itself, not in Meta's read_only_fields or extra_kwargs, which DRF ignores for declared fields."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. ModelSerializer applies Meta.read_only_fields and Meta.extra_kwargs only to the
// fields it builds from the model; a field the serializer declares (`username = serializers.CharField()`), itself or
// through a base serializer of the run in any module, ignores both, silently (DRF Serializers guide, two notes; DRF
// issues #3533, closed as intended, and #3460). A plain Serializer builds no field from a model and ignores its whole
// Meta. A field listed read-only stays writable, so any client can set it (OWASP API3, mass assignment);
// `extra_kwargs = {"password": {"write_only": True}}` on a declared password leaves it in every response.
// It matches a serializer outside test code (a ModelSerializer, a HyperlinkedModelSerializer, or a plain Serializer)
// with a field x declared as a field call (a rest_framework field or a subclass, a nested serializer of the run, a
// `…Field`/`…Serializer` of another package), its own or the nearest run base serializer's that no class in between
// reassigns (`x = None` removes it), and whose Meta, its own or inherited (`class Meta(Base.Meta)`, or no Meta of its
// own), names x:
//   - in read_only_fields (a list, a tuple, `+`, `*splat`, a module-level constant such as `READONLY`,
//     `Other.Meta.read_only_fields`), unless the declared field is read-only anyway: `read_only=True`, written out or
//     through `**RO` with a module-level `RO = {"read_only": True}`, or a SerializerMethodField, ReadOnlyField,
//     HiddenField, HyperlinkedIdentityField, StringRelatedField or a subclass of one;
//   - as a key of extra_kwargs (a dict literal, `dict(...)` or a module-level constant), unless every option of the
//     entry is one the declared call already passes with the same text (or `read_only: True` on a field read-only
//     anyway, or `required: False` on one with a `default=` or read-only: neither is required anyway), or the entry is
//     empty. A field both lists is reported for read_only_fields only.
// A read_only_fields match gets one of three messages. "Written on purpose" (drop the entry, don't set read_only=True)
// when there is evidence the field is meant to be written: the serializer, a run base whose Meta lists x at the same
// entry, or a run subclass that inherits both the entry and the declaration has a `validate_<x>` method, or reads x
// in its `create`, `update`, `validate`, `save` or `to_internal_value` from an input parameter (`validated_data`,
// `attrs`, `data`, any name but `self` and a `**` one) or `self.validated_data`/`self.initial_data`, by subscript,
// `.get` or `.pop` (a store such as `validated_data["x"] = request.user` is no read); or the field's class is a field
// class of the run with its own or an inherited `to_internal_value` (a parser; a nested serializer is no evidence,
// since a project base serializer overriding to_internal_value, as Tandoor's does, parses every serializer's input).
// Otherwise "set read_only=True if clients must not write it, else drop the entry", worded for a plain Serializer
// when the serializer is one. A subclass that only extends the Meta (`Meta(Base.Meta)`) is no evidence of writes:
// that is also the shape of a forgeable field.
// Once per serializer and field, at the place the fix starts from: the name in the Meta option when that name is
// written in the serializer's own body (its own Meta); else at the field's declaration when the serializer declares
// it; else (both inherited) at the class name, and only when no base serializer already has the same pair of name
// and declaration (that base is reported, not every subclass).
//   class UserSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       username = serializers.CharField(max_length=150)
//       full_name = serializers.SerializerMethodField()
//       class Meta:
//           model = User
//           fields = ["id", "username", "full_name"]
//           read_only_fields = ["username", "full_name"]   reported at "username"; full_name is read-only anyway
//   class SignupSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       password = serializers.CharField(write_only=True)
//       class Meta:
//           model = User
//           fields = ["username", "password"]
//           extra_kwargs = {"username": {"required": True}}  not reported: username is not declared
// Also left alone: a serializer whose own or a run base's `__init__` or `get_fields` reads the option by name
// (a mixin applying read_only_fields to the declared fields itself, as addons-server's version serializer does), or,
// for read_only_fields, sets the field read-only itself (`self.fields["x"].read_only = True`, or that assignment in a
// loop over a literal list of names): the entry is dead but harmless; for read_only_fields, a serializer that
// refuses all input (its own or a run base's `validate`, `to_internal_value` or `run_validation` raises
// unconditionally); test code.
// Gaps: a field declared by two bases in a diamond takes the nearest along each path, not DRF's MRO; a project field
// class whose own __init__ forces read_only is reported; extra_kwargs built by a call other than dict(), a `**`
// splat or a comprehension is not read; writes made outside the serializer (a view's perform_update reading
// `serializer.validated_data["x"]`) or through a helper the method calls are not seen, so such a field gets the
// read_only=True message, which also offers dropping the entry; an `__init__` loop over a constant or a Meta option
// other than by name is not read.

#include "lib/drf.rerail"

// A serializer and its bases may sit in different modules: each serializer and field is judged by symbol (dfm_where),
// and a finding is written at the node of the serializer's own file that dfm_where names (dfm_spot).
.violation DeclaredReadOnlyIgnored(at: node, ser: symbol, x: symbol) "`{ser}` declares `{x}`, so DRF ignores read_only_fields for it and clients can write it. If clients must not write it, set read_only=True on the declared field; else drop the entry."
DeclaredReadOnlyIgnored(at, s, x) :- dfm_where(c, x, "read_only_fields", key), dfm_spot(at, key),
    drf_model_serializer_q(c), !dfm_written(c, x), split_dot(c, _, s).

.violation PlainSerializerReadOnlyIgnored(at: node, ser: symbol, x: symbol) "`{ser}` is a plain Serializer, which ignores Meta, so clients can write `{x}`. If clients must not write it, set read_only=True on the declared field; else drop the entry."
PlainSerializerReadOnlyIgnored(at, s, x) :- dfm_where(c, x, "read_only_fields", key), dfm_spot(at, key),
    !drf_model_serializer_q(c), !dfm_written(c, x), split_dot(c, _, s).

.violation DeclaredReadOnlyWritten(at: node, x: symbol) "`{x}` is written on purpose here; drop it from read_only_fields, which DRF ignores for declared fields. Setting read_only=True instead would break that write."
DeclaredReadOnlyWritten(at, x) :- dfm_where(c, x, "read_only_fields", key), dfm_spot(at, key), dfm_written(c, x).

.violation DeclaredExtraKwargsIgnored(at: node, ser: symbol, x: symbol) "`{ser}` declares `{x}`, so DRF ignores its extra_kwargs entry. Pass these arguments to the declared field and drop the entry; if the field already behaves as intended, only drop the entry."
DeclaredExtraKwargsIgnored(at, s, x) :- dfm_where(c, x, "extra_kwargs", key), dfm_spot(at, key), split_dot(c, _, s).

// ---- declarations ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfm_decl(c, x, o): serializer c's field x is declared as `x = <call>` in o's body (home "o.x"): c's own, else the
// nearest run base serializer that declares it with no class between it and c assigning x.
.decl dfm_decl(c: symbol, x: symbol, o: symbol)
dfm_decl(c, x, c) :- drf_serializer_q(c), drf_decl_own(c, x).
dfm_decl(c, x, b) :- drf_serializer_q(c), drf_anc(c, b), drf_serializer_q(b), drf_decl_own(b, x), !drf_qattr(c, x),
    !dfm_shadowed(c, b, x).
.decl dfm_shadowed(c: symbol, b: symbol, x: symbol)
dfm_shadowed(c, b, x) :- drf_serializer_q(c), drf_anc(c, m), drf_node_q(m), drf_anc(m, b), drf_serializer_q(b),
    drf_decl_own(b, x), drf_qattr(m, x).
// dfm_fieldish(hd): declaration hd builds a serializer field, so DRF collects it as a declared field: a
// rest_framework field or a subclass, a nested serializer of the run, or a `…Field`/`…Serializer` class from another
// package. A class of the run that derives from no DRF class (InvenTree's OptionalField, a placeholder its mixin
// swaps for a field) is not one.
.decl dfm_fieldish(hd: symbol)
dfm_fieldish(hd) :- drf_decl_lib_q(hd, _).
dfm_fieldish(hd) :- drf_decl_nested_q(hd, _).
dfm_fieldish(hd) :- dfm_named_field(hd), !dfm_run_callee(hd).
// dfm_named_field(hd): the call home hd holds is a `…Field` or `…Serializer` by its callee's last name.
.decl dfm_named_field(hd: symbol)
dfm_named_field(hd) :- drf_hv(hd, v), unparen(v, k), kind(k, "call"), call_name(k, t),
    (suffix("Field", t) ; suffix("Serializer", t)).
// dfm_callee(hd, fc): declaration hd constructs class fc of the run.
.decl dfm_callee(hd: symbol, fc: symbol)
dfm_callee(hd, fc) :- drf_hcall(hd, f), drf_cls_q(f, fc).
.decl dfm_run_callee(hd: symbol)
dfm_run_callee(hd) :- dfm_callee(hd, _).
// dfm_ro(hd): the declared field is read-only whatever Meta says (`read_only=True`, written out or through `**RO`).
.decl dfm_ro_kind(t: symbol)
dfm_ro_kind("SerializerMethodField"). dfm_ro_kind("ReadOnlyField"). dfm_ro_kind("HiddenField").
dfm_ro_kind("HyperlinkedIdentityField"). dfm_ro_kind("StringRelatedField").
.decl dfm_ro(hd: symbol)
dfm_ro(hd) :- drf_kw_q(hd, "read_only", hk), drf_hkind(hk, "true").
dfm_ro(hd) :- drf_decl_kind_q(hd, t), dfm_ro_kind(t).

// dfm_applied(c, o): serializer c, or a class of the run among its bases, has an `__init__` or `get_fields` that
// names option o (`self.Meta.read_only_fields`, `getattr(self.Meta, "read_only_fields", ())`): it applies the option
// itself. Each class's methods are read in its own file (dfm_reads_opt, dfm_refuses_input, dfm_sets_ro).
.decl dfm_applied(c: symbol, o: symbol)
dfm_applied(c, o) :- drf_serializer_q(c), dfm_reads_opt(c, o).
dfm_applied(c, o) :- drf_serializer_q(c), drf_anc(c, b), dfm_reads_opt(b, o).
.decl dfm_reads_opt(b: symbol, o: symbol)
dfm_reads_opt(b, o) :- (m = "__init__" ; m = "get_fields"), drf_own_method(bc, m, f), within(n, f),
    (attr_of(n, _, o) ; str(n, o)), (o = "read_only_fields" ; o = "extra_kwargs"), class_def(bc, b).
// A serializer that refuses all input (its own or a run base's `validate`, `to_internal_value` or `run_validation`
// raises as a statement of its body, as pretix's `raise TypeError("this serializer is readonly")`) writes no field:
// read_only_fields has nothing to protect.
dfm_applied(c, "read_only_fields") :- drf_serializer_q(c), dfm_refuses_input(c).
dfm_applied(c, "read_only_fields") :- drf_serializer_q(c), drf_anc(c, b), dfm_refuses_input(b).
.decl dfm_refuses_input(b: symbol)
dfm_refuses_input(b) :- (m = "validate" ; m = "to_internal_value" ; m = "run_validation"), drf_own_method(bc, m, f),
    field(f, "body", fb), body_stmt(fb, s, _), kind(s, "raise_statement"), class_def(bc, b).
// dfm_ro_set(c, x): serializer c, or a run base, makes field x read-only in its `__init__` or `get_fields`:
// `self.fields["x"].read_only = True` (any receiver of the subscript), or `....fields[name].read_only = True` in a
// `for name in [...]` loop over literal names.
.decl dfm_ro_set(c: symbol, x: symbol)
dfm_ro_set(c, x) :- drf_serializer_q(c), dfm_sets_ro(c, x).
dfm_ro_set(c, x) :- drf_serializer_q(c), drf_anc(c, b), dfm_sets_ro(b, x).
.decl dfm_ro_store(f: node, a: node, s: node)
dfm_ro_store(f, a, s) :- (m = "__init__" ; m = "get_fields"), drf_own_method(_, m, f), within(a, f),
    kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), attr_of(l, sub, "read_only"), kind(sub, "subscript"),
    field(sub, "subscript", s), field(a, "right", r), kind(r, "true").
.decl dfm_sets_ro(b: symbol, x: symbol)
dfm_sets_ro(b, x) :- drf_own_method(bc, _, f), dfm_ro_store(f, _, s), str(s, x), class_def(bc, b).
dfm_sets_ro(b, x) :- drf_own_method(bc, _, f), dfm_ro_store(f, a, s), kind(s, "identifier"), text(s, y),
    kind(fs, "for_statement"), within(a, fs), within(fs, f), field(fs, "left", t), kind(t, "identifier"), text(t, y),
    field(fs, "right", it), drf_str_elem(it, x), class_def(bc, b).

// ---- Meta values -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfm_ser(c): a serializer outside test code.
.decl dfm_ser(c: symbol)
dfm_ser(c) :- drf_serializer_q(c), !drf_qtest(c).

// dfm_ek(c, x, he): serializer c's (inherited) extra_kwargs has an entry for field x, home he.
.decl dfm_ek(c: symbol, x: symbol, he: symbol)
dfm_ek(c, x, he) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_opt(c, "extra_kwargs", d), drf_sub_q(d, x, he).
// dfm_lit(he): the entry's options are written out (a dict literal or `dict(...)`), so the rule reads all of them.
.decl dfm_lit(he: symbol)
dfm_lit(he) :- drf_hkind(he, "dictionary").
dfm_lit(he) :- drf_hcall(he, "builtins.dict").
// dfm_live(c, x, hd): c's entry for x says something declaration hd does not: an option hd does not pass with the
// same text, or options the rule cannot read.
.decl dfm_cand(c: symbol, x: symbol, hd: symbol)
dfm_cand(c, x, hd) :- dfm_ek(c, x, _), dfm_decl(c, x, o), hd = @dot(o, x).
.decl dfm_same(c: symbol, x: symbol, key: symbol)
dfm_same(c, x, key) :- dfm_cand(c, x, hd), drf_extra_kw_q(c, x, key, hv), drf_kw_q(hd, key, hk), drf_htext(hk, t),
    drf_htext(hv, t).
dfm_same(c, x, "read_only") :- dfm_cand(c, x, hd), drf_extra_kw_q(c, x, "read_only", hv), drf_hkind(hv, "true"),
    dfm_ro(hd).
// A field with a default (or a read-only one) is already not required: `required: False` asks nothing new.
dfm_same(c, x, "required") :- dfm_cand(c, x, hd), drf_extra_kw_q(c, x, "required", hv), drf_hkind(hv, "false"),
    (drf_kw_q(hd, "default", _) ; dfm_ro(hd)).
.decl dfm_live(c: symbol, x: symbol, hd: symbol)
dfm_live(c, x, hd) :- dfm_cand(c, x, hd), drf_extra_kw_q(c, x, key, _), !dfm_same(c, x, key).
dfm_live(c, x, hd) :- dfm_cand(c, x, hd), dfm_ek(c, x, he), !dfm_lit(he).

// ---- hits and where they are reported ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfm_rhit(c, x, w, o): serializer c's read_only_fields names its declared, writable field x (declared in o's body) by
// a string written in home w (the Meta option, a base's, or a module constant: drf_strs).
.decl dfm_rhit(c: symbol, x: symbol, w: symbol, o: symbol)
dfm_rhit(c, x, w, o) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_opt_str(c, "read_only_fields", x, w), dfm_decl(c, x, o), hd = @dot(o, x),
    dfm_fieldish(hd), !dfm_ro(hd), !dfm_applied(c, "read_only_fields"), !dfm_ro_set(c, x).
.decl dfm_rof_hit(c: symbol, x: symbol)
dfm_rof_hit(c, x) :- dfm_rhit(c, x, _, _).
// dfm_hit(c, x, opt, w, o): serializer c's Meta option opt names its declared field x (declared in o's body),
// uselessly, by a string or an entry written in home w.
.decl dfm_hit(c: symbol, x: symbol, opt: symbol, w: symbol, o: symbol)
dfm_hit(c, x, "read_only_fields", w, o) :- dfm_rhit(c, x, w, o).
dfm_hit(c, x, "extra_kwargs", he, o) :- dfm_ek(c, x, he), dfm_decl(c, x, o), hd = @dot(o, x), dfm_fieldish(hd),
    dfm_live(c, x, hd), !dfm_applied(c, "extra_kwargs"), !dfm_rof_hit(c, x).
// A base serializer of c with the same pair is reported itself; c, inheriting both, is not.
.decl dfm_inherited(c: symbol, x: symbol, opt: symbol)
dfm_inherited(c, x, opt) :- dfm_hit(c, x, opt, w, o), drf_anc(c, b), dfm_hit(b, x, opt, w, o).
// dfm_where(c, x, opt, key): where the finding goes, as a dfm_spot key: the name in the Meta option when it is written
// in c's own body (its home under c); else c's own declaration of x; else (both inherited) c's name, unless a base
// with the same pair is reported.
.decl dfm_where(c: symbol, x: symbol, opt: symbol, key: symbol)
dfm_where(c, x, "read_only_fields", cat("str|", w, "|", x)) :- dfm_hit(c, x, "read_only_fields", w, _),
    prefix(cat(c, "."), w).
dfm_where(c, x, "extra_kwargs", cat("entry|", w)) :- dfm_hit(c, x, "extra_kwargs", w, _), prefix(cat(c, "."), w).
dfm_where(c, x, opt, cat("decl|", c, ".", x)) :- dfm_hit(c, x, opt, w, c), !prefix(cat(c, "."), w).
dfm_where(c, x, opt, cat("name|", c)) :- dfm_hit(c, x, opt, w, _), !prefix(cat(c, "."), w), !drf_qattr(c, x),
    !dfm_inherited(c, x, opt).
// dfm_spot(at, key): the nodes a finding can go at: a string holding x in home w's value ("str|w|x"); the key of an
// extra_kwargs entry he (or, for `dict(x=...)`, its value: "entry|he"); the statement `x = …` of class c ("decl|c.x");
// class c's name ("name|c").
.decl dfm_spot(at: node, key: symbol)
dfm_spot(e, cat("str|", w, "|", x)) :- drf_hv(w, v), drf_vlit_at(v, e, x).
dfm_spot(e, cat("entry|", he)) :- drf_hsubv(he, ov), kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "value", ov), field(p, "key", e).
dfm_spot(ov, cat("entry|", he)) :- drf_hsubv(he, ov), kind(p, "keyword_argument"), field(p, "value", ov).
dfm_spot(a, cat("decl|", c, ".", x)) :- class_def(k, c), drf_own_attr(k, x, _, a).
dfm_spot(n, cat("name|", c)) :- class_def(k, c), field(k, "name", n).

// ---- written on purpose ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfm_carrier(c, x, h): serializer h shares c's read_only_fields entry for x: c itself, a run base whose Meta lists x
// by the same string (written in the same home), or a run subclass with the same entry and declaration.
.decl dfm_carrier(c: symbol, x: symbol, h: symbol)
dfm_carrier(c, x, c) :- dfm_rhit(c, x, _, _).
dfm_carrier(c, x, b) :- dfm_rhit(c, x, w, _), drf_anc(c, b), drf_opt_str(b, "read_only_fields", x, w).
dfm_carrier(c, x, s) :- dfm_rhit(c, x, w, o), drf_anc(s, c), dfm_rhit(s, x, w, o).
// dfm_written(c, x): some carrier writes x on purpose, or the field's class (a field, not a serializer) parses input.
.decl dfm_written(c: symbol, x: symbol)
dfm_written(c, x) :- dfm_carrier(c, x, h), dfm_writes(h, x).
dfm_written(c, x) :- dfm_rhit(c, x, _, o), hd = @dot(o, x), dfm_callee(hd, fc), !drf_serializer_q(fc),
    drf_method_q(fc, "to_internal_value", _).
.decl dfm_in_method(m: symbol)
dfm_in_method("create"). dfm_in_method("update"). dfm_in_method("validate"). dfm_in_method("save").
dfm_in_method("to_internal_value").
.decl dfm_writes(h: symbol, x: symbol)
dfm_writes(h, x) :- dfm_carrier(_, x, h), drf_qmethod(h, m, _), m = cat("validate_", x).
dfm_writes(h, x) :- dfm_carrier(_, x, h), drf_qmethod(h, m, fq), dfm_in_method(m), dfm_reads_key(fq, x).
// dfm_in_fn(f): an input method of a class (create, update, validate, save, to_internal_value).
.decl dfm_in_fn(f: node)
dfm_in_fn(f) :- drf_own_method(_, m, f), dfm_in_method(m).
// dfm_input(o, f): expression o in method f holds the input: a parameter (not self, not a `**` one), or
// self.validated_data / self.initial_data.
.decl dfm_input(o: node, f: node)
dfm_input(o, f) :- dfm_in_fn(f), within(o, f), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, y), param(f, y, _), y != "self",
    !dfm_kwsplat(f, y).
dfm_input(o, f) :- dfm_in_fn(f), within(o, f), attr_of(o, s, a), kind(s, "identifier"), text(s, "self"),
    (a = "validated_data" ; a = "initial_data").
.decl dfm_kwsplat(f: node, y: symbol)
dfm_kwsplat(f, y) :- dfm_in_fn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), kind(p, "dictionary_splat_pattern"),
    child(p, id, 0), text(id, y).
// dfm_reads_key(fq, x): method fq reads key x of its input: `o["x"]` (not as an assignment target), `o.get("x")`,
// `o.pop("x")`.
.decl dfm_reads_key(fq: symbol, x: symbol)
dfm_reads_key(fq, x) :- dfm_input(o, f), field(n, "value", o), kind(n, "subscript"), field(n, "subscript", s),
    str(s, x), !dfm_store(n), qualname(f, fq).
dfm_reads_key(fq, x) :- dfm_input(o, f), attr_of(fn, o, m), (m = "get" ; m = "pop"), field(n, "function", fn),
    kind(n, "call"), call_arg(n, 0, "", a), str(a, x), qualname(f, fq).
.decl dfm_store(n: node)
dfm_store(n) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", n), kind(n, "subscript").
dfm_store(n) :- kind(a, "augmented_assignment"), field(a, "left", n), kind(n, "subscript").

// The cases, `cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "core/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/core/__init__.py"
    .fixture "core/fields.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/core/fields.py"
    .fixture "core/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/core/serializers.py"
    .fixture "accounts/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/models.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/models.py"
    .fixture "accounts/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/serializers.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/test_serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/tests/test_serializers.py"
    .fixture "writes/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/writes/__init__.py"
